 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nTabStops indexing and length calculation broken\n\n#### Description\n\nThe TabStops class has issues with indexing and length calculation. When trying to access tab stops by index or get the length of a TabStops object, unexpected behavior occurs.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom docx import Document\nfrom docx.shared import Inches\n\n# Create a document and add some tab stops\ndoc = Document()\nparagraph = doc.add_paragraph()\ntab_stops = paragraph.paragraph_format.tab_stops\n\n# Add a tab stop\ntab_stops.add_tab_stop(Inches(1))\n\n# Try to get the length - this returns wrong value\nprint(f\"Length: {len(tab_stops)}\")  # Expected: 1, but gets different value\n\n# Try to access by index - this fails\ntry:\n    first_tab = tab_stops[0]\n    print(f\"First tab position: {first_tab.position}\")\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f\"Error accessing tab stop: {e}\")\n\n# Try with empty tab stops\nempty_paragraph = doc.add_paragraph()\nempty_tab_stops = empty_paragraph.paragraph_format.tab_stops\n\ntry:\n    empty_tab = empty_tab_stops[0]\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f\"Error with empty tab stops: {e}\")  # Should be IndexError but gets different error\n```\n\nThe indexing seems to be off by one and the length calculation is incorrect. Also, accessing empty TabStops raises the wrong exception type.\n</issue>\n",
